 <iati-activity default-currency="USD" hierarchy="1" humanitarian="0" iati-activities:version="2.03" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities" xmlns:iom="http://iom.int">
  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-47066-NC.0158</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assessing the Implications of Climate Change Loss and Damage on Human Mobility in Latin America</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As climate change impacts worsen across the world, the international debate on climate action has increasingly included loss and damage considerations from a climate justice perspective. As mobility considerations have been included in the loss and damage work of the UNFCCC, it becomes important to better assess the implications of climate change loss and damage on different forms of human mobility. In this context, the project aims to enhance governmental capacity in formulating and implementing/funding policies on climate-induced mobility by creating a relevant and participatory tool to assess the implications of loss and damage (both economic and non-economic) associated to climate mobility in Latin America.</narrative>
  </description>
